WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.367
Some big

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.201
news announced from

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.635
the Biden administration today.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.705
The Taliban has killed an ISIS leader.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.240
According to Biden administration

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.475
officials, that leader

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.510
is the same person who planned

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.013
the deadly attack on American troops

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.448
and Afghan civilians at the Kabul airport

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.649
during the chaotic U.S.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.451
withdrawal from the country.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.153
13 American servicemen

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:20.787
as you'll remember,

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.423
and more than 170 Afghans were killed

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.992
in that bombing back in 20, 21.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:26.593
Joining me now

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.094
from the White House is John Kirby,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:28.628
the coordinator

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.896
for strategic communications

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.664
for the National Security Council.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.067
John, thank you for coming for coming on.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.803
What more can you tell us about this?

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.705
What was this ISIS leader's name?

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.807
How was he killed?

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.876
Well, we're not at liberty to talk

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.811
about his specific name

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.347
necessarily, Kate, but we are confident,

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:48.748
based on information

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.517
that we've been able to glean

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.785
that this is the individual

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.686
who was, as we've called him,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.487
the mastermind

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.889
of that Abigail Gate attack.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.657
And, of course, our condolences.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:58.024
Our thoughts

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.659
and prayers continue to go out

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.527
to all the families

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.095
of those 13 servicemembers lost,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.096
as well as

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:03.863
the family members

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.331
of the Afghan victims

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.200
of that terrible, terrible day.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.035
But we know that the Taliban took

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.070
this individual out,

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.538
killed him in an operation

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.273
that they were conducting on their own

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.274
without any assistance,

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.842
certainly from the United States.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.476
And it's important,

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.811
I think, for viewers to remember

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.779
that the Taliban and ISIS

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.881
are mortal enemies there in Afghanistan.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.683
They continue to fight one another,

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.451
as a matter of fact.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.653
Now, this is the third senior leader

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.988
that the Taliban have killed in terms of

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.224
ISI's key leadership.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.158
John, can you talk to me

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.827
about the hesitancy to talk in

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.662
releasing the leader's name?

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.763
I was just looking this morning

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.063
and saw

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.265
back in the beginning of April, CENTCOM

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.500
when a press release

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.001
very clearly named

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.137
another another ISIS leader that was

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.105
taken out in Syria.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.740
Yeah, I wish I could give you

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.709
more context to your Kate

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.578
We're just not able to speak publicly

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.046
about the name right now.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.248
There's there's reasons for that.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.216
But I can tell you

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.083
that we're confident

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.818
that this is the individual

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:01.321
who in fact, masterminded that attack.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.490
John, after the Abigail attack,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.491
everyone will remember

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.693
President Biden's speech that night

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.161
and he vowed retribution.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.362
I mean, he said,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.931
we will not forgive, we will not forget.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:14.701
We will hunt you down and make you pay.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:15.301
The fact

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.369
that the Taliban is

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.072
who killed this leader does

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.674
does this speak to the limits of U.S.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.209
capabilities in Afghanistan

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.878
after the withdrawal?

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.346
No, actually,

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.480
I think it validates

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.481
the president's decision

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.183
to leave Afghanistan altogether.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.951
You don't need to have a big presence

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.987
on the ground, boots on the ground

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.321
to go after terrorist threats,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.723
whether they're in Afghanistan

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.290
or elsewhere,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:37.891
and look

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.559
the Taliban killed this individual.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.494
I think it's a good thing that he's gone.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.495
I think it's a great thing

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.097
that he's no longer walking the earth

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.832
and no longer can plan attacks

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.666
and conduct attacks

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.401
against anyone let alone

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.769
American interests.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.436
But, look,

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.438
I think it's also important to remember

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.907
we killed al-Zawahiri

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.208
while he was sitting on a balcony

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.843
in Kabul, Afghanistan,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.878
using over the horizon capabilities.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.280
And we've taken out other ISIS

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.481
leaders in Somalia

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.049
and in Syria, again,

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.050
using over the horizon.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.151
What the president said at

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.085
also that day

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.654
was that we're going to make sure

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.855
we can continue to sharpen

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.856
and improve our abilities

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.089
to go

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.658
after these guys in an over

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.593
the horizon, low footprint way.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.261
And we've actually proven that case time

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.330
and time again with this

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.065
Does does

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.666
it does

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.768
President Biden, despite administration,

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.570
trust the Taliban

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.938
any more today than they did

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.739
previous to this?

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:27.740
No, ma'am.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.009
This is not this is not about trust.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:30.944
Not at all.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.011
And we didn't

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.946
we weren't involved in this.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:35.048
We didn't partner with them on this.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:35.815
They have said

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.250
they said in their agreement

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.651
which they signed under the Trump

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.786
administration, that they were going

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.988
to not allow Afghanistan to become a safe

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.157
haven for al Qaeda or terrorist networks.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:44.857
We're going to hold them

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:45.992
to that commitment.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.860
We want to see them meet that commitment.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.395
But this is not about trust, not now.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.130
Not the way that the Taliban

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.198
is treating its own people,

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:52.899
women and girls.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.366
I mean,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.500
they are not meeting

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.235
all their commitments

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.402
to the international community.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.870
And we we're going to continue

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.105
to urge them to do that.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:03:59.973
Oren Liebermann

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.641
has been following the reaction and joins

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.010
us now from the Pentagon.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.311
So are in the mastermind

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.247
behind the Kabul attack

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.915
that left these 13 U.S.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:09.682
servicemen dead.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.018
These 170 Afghans killed.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.121
He's now dead, killed by the Taliban.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.656
How is the Pentagon reacting?

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.057
What are they saying?

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.058
Well, it's interesting.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.760
We got a statement fairly late last night

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.761
from the Defense Department,

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.929
which says that the United States

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.098
had no role in this operation

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.733
or whatever happened there

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.800
that led to the death

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.902
of the senior ISI's leader.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.804
So that's telling in and of itself

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.106
that there was no coordination

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.507
or cooperation with the Taliban,

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.074
at least according

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.242
to the Defense Department.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:36.743
In what

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.678
led to the death of this ISIS leader.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:39.545
Although the White House

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.180
didn't say when this had happened.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.415
DOD saying this happened

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.250
sometime in early April.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:44.884
What's unclear

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.053
is how exactly the Taliban killed

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.388
this senior ISIS leader,

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.390
whether it was a targeted attack

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.158
they were going after this leader

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.760
or whether it was simply infighting

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.162
between Isaac and the Taliban.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.398
Last month, it was General Eric Carillo,

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.232
the commander of U.S.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.700
Central Command, who said the ISI's K

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.535
has been carrying out more attacks

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.236
throughout the region

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.304
in which they are active.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.405
That is Afghanistan.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.440
And some of the surrounding countries,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.142
but also that their goal

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.243
was to attack U.S.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.512
interests outside of Afghanistan.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.379
Although ultimately,

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:13.680
he says

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.480
they'd like to carry out

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.449
an attack on the U.S. homeland.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.151
They are far from being able to do so

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.552
and would more likely try to target U.S.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.553
interests abroad.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.454
Broadly speaking,

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.156
that seeks to isolate Kaye's intent.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:23.723
But the White House

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.792
saying this is one of several senior

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.660
ISIS leaders who has been killed

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.262
since the beginning of the year.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.030
Even those who were critical of the U.S.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.565
withdrawal from Afghanistan

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.167
have praised the death

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.668
of this senior ISIS leader.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.769
For example, Representative

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.770
Michael McCaul,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.172
the Republican head of the House

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.673
Foreign Relations Committee,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.542
says this is one terrorist dead

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.310
and that itself is a good thing.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.311
But it doesn't absolve

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.479
the Biden administration

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.780
from the responsibility

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.349
of how the withdrawal from Afghanistan

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.617
was handled and the deaths of the 13 U.S.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.786
service members and more than 170 Afghans

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.888
in that suicide bombing

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.690
in the closing days of the withdrawal.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.391
In fact, CNN

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.058
also spoke

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.093
with a father

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.294
of one of the Marines who was killed

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.128
in that attack,

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.830
who had largely the same sentiment.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.697
It's good that

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.865
that the world

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.433
got rid of a terrorist in this case.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.101
But again,

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.268
what he wants to see

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.237
is more more accountability,

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.538
more responsibility taken from

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.840
not only the White House,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.841
but also the Pentagon.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:17.076
And the State Department. Linda?

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:17.377
Yeah,

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:18.678
and of course, Ana, to talk to us

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.680
more about that,

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.614
given the fact that the U.S.

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:22.882
is now out of Afghanistan,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:23.883
how difficult it

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.551
how challenging it is

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.687
to gather intelligence for the U.S.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:30.223
and its allies on ISIS,

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:34.293
on other terrorism related groups?

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.461
Right now, given

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.963
they don't really have a presence there?

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:38.865
It's much more

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.099
difficult because it has to be done

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.034
essentially from above.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.070
Spy satellites and drones flown, flown

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:44.904
in from far away.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.005
And what the Biden administration

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:46.739
has called

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.875
its over the horizon capability.

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:50.309
They point to

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.178
a very small number of actions

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.479
that the U.S. has taken.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.514
The the

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:55.281
the targeted

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.949
killing, the assassination of Zawahiri

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.885
in Kabul several months ago.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.120
But there isn't much more to look at

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.455
in terms of

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.556
kinetic activity

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:04.590
that the Biden administration

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.491
has as carried out

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.126
since the withdrawal from Afghanistan.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.094
And General Chiarelli,

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:09.328
again, the commander of U.S.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.763
Central Command, has pointed out

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:12.698
it is much harder to gather intel

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.400
to act on that intel

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.601
now that the U.S. is out.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.803
So that remains

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.704
one of the ongoing challenges

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.072
for the military and more broadly

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.541
for the U.S..

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.309
Oren Liebermann for us at the Pentagon,

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:24.777
good to have you with us. Thanks so much.

